-- title:
--   Hecke operator at ℓ commutes with a diamond operator
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$, a commutative ring $\kappa$ and a $\kappa$-linear representation $X$ of the group $\Gamma_H(N)$ for $H=\bot$, i.e. of the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH N ⊥`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ consisting of those elements of $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose image under [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) (the lower-right entry viewed as a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/N$) is trivial. Let $M$ be a submonoid of the monoid of $2\times 2$ integer matrices containing the underlying matrix of every element of $\Gamma_0(N)$ (hypothesis $h\Gamma$), and let $\rho' : M \to \operatorname{End}_\kappa X$ be a monoid homomorphism such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_H(N)$ the action $X.\rho\,\gamma$ equals $\rho'$ applied to the matrix of $\gamma$. Let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $N$ with $\mathrm{diag}(\ell,1) \in M$, and let $\sigma \in \Gamma_0(N)$. Two twisting hypotheses are assumed, both instances of [`HeckeCohomology.IsTwist`](def/GroupCohomology_TransferHecke.html#L12): first, that $\varphi = \rho'(\mathrm{diag}(\ell,1))$ satisfies $\varphi(X.\rho(c\,s)\,a) = X.\rho(s)(\varphi\,a)$ for all $a \in X$ and all $s$ in the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaHUpper N ⊥ ℓ`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L210) of $\Gamma_H(N)$ (those elements whose upper-right entry vanishes mod $\ell$), where $c$ is [`HeckeCohomology.cTop N ⊥ ℓ`](def/GroupCohomology_DClassCoeff.html#L33), the homomorphism $s \mapsto \mathrm{conjUpperMat}\,\ell\,s$ of [`CohCarrier.conjL`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L228) corestricted to the top subgroup of $\Gamma_H(N)$; second, that $\psi = \rho'(\sigma^{-1})$ satisfies $\psi(X.\rho(\sigma\gamma\sigma^{-1})\,a) = X.\rho(\gamma)(\psi\,a)$ for all $\gamma \in \Gamma_H(N)$ and $a \in X$, the map $\gamma \mapsto \sigma\gamma\sigma^{-1}$ being [`CohCarrier.conjHom N ⊥ σ`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L284) regarded as an endomorphism of the top subgroup. The conclusion is that the two induced $\kappa$-linear endomorphisms of $H^1(\Gamma_H(N), X)$ produced by [`HeckeCohomology.heckeH1`](def/GroupCohomology_TransferHecke.html#L162) from these data, namely the one attached to $(c,\varphi)$ and the one attached to $(\gamma \mapsto \sigma\gamma\sigma^{-1}, \psi)$, commute with one another.
--
--   This is the commutation of the Hecke operator $T_\ell$ with the diamond operator $\langle\sigma\rangle$ on the first cohomology of $\Gamma_1(N)$ with coefficients in $X$, realised here through twisted transfer maps on $H^1$. It feeds the statement [`HeckeCohomology.commute_of_forall_eq_heckeH1_cTop_or_eq_heckeH1_conjHom_of_forall_rep_eq_monoidHom_submonoid`](thm.html#HeckeCohomology.commute_of_forall_eq_heckeH1_cTop_or_eq_heckeH1_conjHom_of_forall_rep_eq_monoidHom_submonoid), from which commutativity of the whole algebra generated by these operators is obtained.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HeckeCohomology_commute_heckeH1_cTop_heckeH1_conjHom_of_forall_rep_eq_monoidHom_submonoid.lean

